      "text": "To determine the value of \\(A + H\\) in the sequence \\(A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H\\) with \\(C = 5\\) and the sum of any three consecutive terms equal to 30, we start by writing out the equations based on the given information.\n\nWe know:\n\\[\nA + B + C = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nB + C + D = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nC + D + E = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nD + E + F = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nE + F + G = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nF + G + H = 30\n\\]\n\nFrom the first equation, we can express \\(B\\) in terms of \\(A\\) and \\(C\\):\n\\[\nB = 30 - A - C\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(C = 5\\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\nB = 30 - A - 5 = 25 - A\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(B\\) and \\(C\\) into the second equation:\n\\[\n25 - A + 5 + D = 30\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n30 - A + D = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nD = A\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\(D = A\\) into the third equation:\n\\[\n5 + A + E = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nE = 25 - A\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(D\\) and \\(E\\) into the fourth equation:\n\\[\nA + 25 - A + F = 30\n\\]\n\\[\n25 + F = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nF = 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\(F = 5\\) into the fifth equation:\n\\[\n5 + 5 + G = 30\n\\]\n\\[\n10 + G = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nG = 20\n\\]\n\nFinally, we substitute \\(F = 5\\) and \\(G = 20\\) into the sixth equation:\n\\[\n5 + 20 + H = 30\n\\]\n\\[\n25 + H = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nH = 5\n\\]\n\nSince we are asked to find \\(A + H\\), and we have determined that \\(H = 5\\), the final answer is:\n\\[\nA + H = A + 5\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(A + H\\) is \\(\\boxed{25}\\).",
