      "text": "Given the sequence \\(A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H\\) with the conditions that \\(C = 5\\) and the sum of any three consecutive terms is 30, we need to find the value of \\(A + H\\).\n\nFirst, we can write out the given conditions mathematically:\n\\[A + B + C = 30\\]\n\\[B + C + D = 30\\]\n\\[C + D + E = 30\\]\n\\[D + E + F = 30\\]\n\\[E + F + G = 30\\]\n\\[F + G + H = 30\\]\n\nSimplifying these conditions, we get:\n1. \\(A + B + 5 = 30 \\implies A + B = 25\\)\n2. \\(B + 5 + D = 30 \\implies B + D = 25\\)\n3. \\(5 + D + E = 30 \\implies D + E = 25\\)\n4. \\(D + E + F = 30 \\implies D + E + F = 30\\)\n5. \\(E + F + G = 30 \\implies E + F + G = 30\\)\n6. \\(F + G + H = 30 \\implies F + G + H = 30\\)\n\nFrom equations 1 and 2, we can express \\(B\\) and \\(D\\) in terms of \\(A\\) and \\(E\\):\n\\[B = 25 - A\\]\n\\[D = 25 - B = 25 - (25 - A) = A\\]\n\nFrom equations 3 and 4, we can express \\(D\\) and \\(E\\) in terms of \\(A\\) and \\(C\\):\n\\[D = A\\]\n\\[E = 25 - D = 25 - A\\]\n\nFrom equations 5 and 6, we can express \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) in terms of \\(A\\) and \\(C\\):\n\\[E = 25 - A\\]\n\\[F = 30 - E = 30 - (25 - A) = A + 5\\]\n\nFrom equations 7, we can express \\(F\\) and \\(G\\) in terms of \\(A\\) and \\(D\\):\n\\[F = A + 5\\]\n\\[G = 30 - F = 30 - (A + 5) = 25 - A\\]\n\nFrom equations 8, we can express \\(G\\) and \\(H\\) in terms of \\(A\\) and \\(C\\):\n\\[G = 25 - A\\]\n\\[H = 30 - G = 30 - (25 - A) = A + 5\\]\n\nNow that we have all the terms rearranged in terms of \\(A\\) and \\(C\\):\n\\[A\\]\n\\[25 - A\\]\n\\[A\\]\n\\[D = A\\]\n\\[30 - A\\]\n\\[A + 5\\]\n\\[F = A + 5\\]\n\\[25 - A\\]\n\\[H = A + 5\\]\n\nSince \\(D = A\\) and \\(F = A + 5\\), and there's no direct reference to \\(A\\) and \\(H\\) in these terms, the only necessary values we need are \\(A\\) and \\(H\\), which are both \\(25 + D + C = 25 + A + 5 = 30 + A\\).\n\nFrom the equations where we solved for \\(D\\) and \\(C\\), the only necessary values for \\(A\\) and \\(H\\) due to the sum of the sequence's conditions is:\n\\[A = 20\\]\n\\[H = 10\\]\n\nThus, \\(A + H = 20 + 10 = 30\\).\n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{30}\\).",
